// REQUIRES: e2e
// RUN: %jocky build "%S/../../forensic/mem/jocky-mem.jk" -o "%t.exe" -L %jockyrt_libdir -l jockyrt
// RUN: "%t.exe" selftest | %FileCheck "%s"
// RUN: %not "%t.exe" inventory 999999 | %FileCheck --check-prefix=BADPID "%s"
//
// Builds the real forensic tool (forensic/mem/jocky-mem.jk) and exercises two
// paths: `selftest` inventories this very process (proving open + region walk +
// module classification work), and a bogus pid must fail cleanly rather than
// hang - a regression guard for the FFI signedness bug where `jkf_open`'s C
// `int` -5 was read as a 64-bit value with garbage in the high word, so
// `h < 0` came out false and the region loop spun forever.
//
// CHECK: SELFTEST OK
//
// BADPID: cannot open pid 999999 (error -5)
